WEBVTT

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:03.480
Found you.

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.200
I found the intruder.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:09.490
Huh? There are two, but I guess that's okay.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:11.850
<i>This girl...</i>

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:14.130
<i>She's one of the ones who kidnapped Miyu.</i>

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:16.190
<i>Wh-What do I do?</i>

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:18.220
<i>And Ruby's not here...</i>

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:51.630
<b>Episode 2 
Encounters and Reunions</b>

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:54.910
Why don't you come out of there?

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:56.880
I won't hurt you.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:00.260
Tanaka-san, go out through the back and run!

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:01.310
Tanaka-san?

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:03.060
Tana—

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:07.100
I'm Tanaka! Where are we? Who am I?

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:07.100
Tanaka-san?!

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:09.210
Bloomers?!

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:10.730
Idiot! Pervert!

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:13.630
What's with this girl?

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:15.710
Did we have someone like her?

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:17.440
Well, whatever.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.110
For now...

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:20.280
A Card!

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:22.370
<i>Include!</i>

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:29.600
Oh!

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:30.120
Huh?

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:33.390
Let's go a round!

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:39.970
Ah, there's the white one.

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:43.500
W-We have to run, Tanaka-san! Run!

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:48.550
You're running?

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:51.610
Good... I enjoy that, too.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:56.110
<i>That woman Included the Card into her arm?</i>

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.730
<i>Berserker? A second one?</i>

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:01.200
<i>Plus, does "white one" mean...</i>

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:03.820
<i>No, right now,</i>

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:05.220
<i>I have to run!</i>

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:10.120
I'm good at cornering people who run...

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:12.120
And I love it!

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:23.300
Oh, come on. You have totally no fight in you.

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:30.310
I wanted to throw more things at you.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:34.940
Tanaka-san?

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:38.030
What? If you're going to beg for your life,

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:40.190
I'd prefer if you were as pitiful as possible.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:41.450
Um...

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:43.540
Who am I?

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:45.510
Like I know! You're an idiot!

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:47.080
You're a supreme idiot!

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:50.970
Tanaka-san! Please realize what's happening!

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:53.040
In that case...

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.670
Who are you?

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:58.130
Well, fine.

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:00.960
It seems dumb to give my name to an idiot, but...

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:03.840
I'm Beatrice Flowerchild!

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:06.880
Ainsworth's supremely beautiful doll!

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:08.930
Glad to know ya!

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:10.470
<i>"Ainsworth"...</i>

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:12.320
<i>Tanaka-san just mentioned that.</i>

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:14.560
<i>Then these people really are...</i>

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:16.560
Ainsworth...

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:24.450
That said, we'll only know each other 
for about one second longer!

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:29.790
What? I was just at the super good part!

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.180
Yeah, that's true, but...

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:36.960
Yes, yes. I know!

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:38.920
<i>She's talking to someone?</i>

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.900
Tsk, fine.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:42.900
I'll see you two again.

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:45.140
Next time, I'll definitely crush you dead!

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:46.260
Ah!

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:47.950
She's gone?

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:53.270
That was a surprise. Now, shall we get going?

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:54.100
Huh?

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.190
Wh-Where?

00:04:56.910 --> 00:05:00.400
Illya-san, you're searching for Miyu, right?

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:05.780
Yeah, that person just now captured 
Miyu, so I have to go save her!

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:09.500
Okay! Then I'll go with you, too.

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:13.410
Th-Thank you... But why?

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:17.400
Because my role is to eliminate 
the Ainsworth family.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.100
Wow, really?

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:20.840
Huh?

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:24.050
Wh-What do you mean by that, Tanaka-san?

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:25.820
I'm not sure.

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:29.510
I still don't remember much,
except just one thing...

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:32.680
I absolutely must destroy that family.

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:35.480
For whatever reason, that's all I can remember.

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:42.140
<i>Frankly, there's still too much 
I don't understand,</i>

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:46.450
<i>but it seems to be true that Tanaka-san 
and I have the same destination.</i>

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:49.320
Let's go, Tanaka-san.

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:51.160
Where's the Ainsworth family?

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:56.550
I don't know.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:00.780
Right. You have amnesia.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:03.550
It's not your fault.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:08.760
Thinking for even one second that 
I could rely on you was my mistake.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:11.260
Am I being blamed?

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:13.930
What do I do from here?

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:17.100
I don't even know where our destination is...

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:21.230
Hey, Tanaka-san, do you have any 
memories that might give us a clue?

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:23.670
Tanaka-san?!

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:25.690
What's wrong, Tanaka-san?

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:29.170
M-My tummy is sad.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:35.120
Oh... That's right, you haven't 
had anything but water.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.760
Please take me to the park.

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:39.800
Water? You plan to drink water?!

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:41.660
I'm sorry, Tanaka-san!

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:45.500
I didn't tell you, but you can't relieve 
real hunger with water!

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:47.340
Wh-What do I do?

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.470
Where do I go for food?

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:53.400
What's wrong? On the verge of collapse?

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:54.370
Huh?

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:02.480
Something smells good!

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.110
Oh, you're awake.

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:07.050
Huh? Where are we?

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:08.400
At a ramen shop.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:11.860
The owner helped carry you here 
while you were unconscious.

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:13.630
It's almost done.

00:07:13.630 --> 00:07:15.370
Sit quietly and wait.

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:17.660
Um, I'm sorry.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:21.300
You helped me carry Tanaka-san, 
and now you're treating us to food.

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:23.030
I don't mind.

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:24.530
You were hungry, right?

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:27.070
As a ramen shop owner, 
I couldn't leave you there.

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:30.310
It smells real good! What is it?

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:32.720
You don't know what ramen is?

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:34.290
I don't!

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:36.550
It smells like you crushed wheat into powder,

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:40.600
kneaded it with water, 
and boiled the solid result!

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.800
What's with her?

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:45.920
She has a very slanted breadth of knowledge.

00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:47.600
It's done.

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:49.520
Feel free to savor it.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:53.670
Yay! Thank you very much! Now, to eat...

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:56.610
It's red.

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:59.760
Um, what's this?

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:00.750
Hmm?

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:02.690
It's mapo tofu.

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:04.500
Where's the ramen?

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:06.200
The noodles are just decoration.

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:09.880
There's only a paltry amount, 
sunk within a mapo sea.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:12.020
Huh?! There isn't even any ramen broth!

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:14.010
It's all just mapo sauce!

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:20.920
And it's as spicy as it looks!

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:22.770
It's hellishly spicy!

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:25.690
You complain a lot.

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:28.180
Why don't you learn from your companion?

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:33.370
Thank you so much.

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:38.610
My mouth and stomach are so 
burned, they're throbbing,

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:40.340
and I can't stop sweating or shaking.

00:08:40.340 --> 00:08:42.650
That's not an opinion on the food!

00:08:42.650 --> 00:08:45.000
Well, it goes without saying,

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:47.320
but I won't let you leave any uneaten.

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:49.170
If you say it's impossible to eat,

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:53.090
I'll bury you up to your neck and 
pour the mapo down your throat.

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:56.760
I don't want to become a delicacy!

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:01.000
Thank you for the food...

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:01.770
Good.

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:03.180
Enjoy it, girl.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:06.180
Now you've consumed a whole 
day's worth of calories.

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:08.770
Just how cruel is this meal?!

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:10.980
Um,

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:13.310
would you mind if I asked something?

00:09:13.310 --> 00:09:16.320
What in the world happened to this city?

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:17.850
What do you mean?

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:20.050
That huge crater, for one.

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:24.290
That big hole was caused by a gas explosion.

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:26.250
A gas explosion?

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:28.390
It happened roughly five years ago.

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:32.560
A vast deposit of natural gas sleeping 
in the earth somehow caught fire

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:34.970
and blew away several kilometers.

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:36.970
They issued an evacuation order, as well.

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:41.180
So now, people live meagerly 
on the outskirts of the city.

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:45.060
Uh, in that case, why is it snowing?

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:48.180
Snowing? It always snows in summer.

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:50.370
You can say that with a straight face?

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:51.900
More importantly,

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:55.240
two mapo ramen come to 3,200 yen.

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:57.610
You're charging?

00:09:57.610 --> 00:09:58.600
Of course.

00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:03.220
B-But wouldn't you normally treat us 
after what we went through?

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:04.660
And isn't that expensive?

00:10:05.030 --> 00:10:07.620
Surely you aren't penniless, are you?

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:10.680
T-Tanaka-san, do you have money?

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:14.920
What's money? Does it taste good?

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:16.340
That's what I thought!

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:19.090
You underestimate me if you 
think you can dine and dash.

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:22.100
However, I did just run out of pork bones.

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:25.380
That's way more hostility than a 
ramen shop owner should express!

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:29.720
Consider yourself fortunate that 
your final meal was my mapo

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:30.980
as you leave this life!

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:33.980
Afternoon. Still at it, old man?

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:35.720
Hmm?

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:36.710
Huh?

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:39.260
Oh?

00:10:41.420 --> 00:10:43.080
Good grief...

00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:46.830
What are you doing, after I just paid your bill?

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:49.720
W-Well, you're our enemy, aren't you?

00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:53.090
You're the Heroic Spirit of the 
Card, so you're after Miyu?

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:55.200
That's uncouth...

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:57.840
Bringing that up again, after you won?

00:10:58.210 --> 00:11:01.230
That bit ended in your victory, didn't it?

00:11:01.230 --> 00:11:05.440
Besides, I was just respecting 
the will of my "black" self.

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:09.020
I, personally, have no reason to oppose you.

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:13.690
Why are you alive, anyway?

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:18.110
Because you only blasted away my "black" self.

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:22.250
So while I was wandering that 
mountain searching for something,

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:25.160
I was accidentally swept up in the dimension shift.

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:27.370
Before I knew it, I was here.

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:28.620
So,

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:31.990
let's get along from now on, Onee-chan.

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:41.870
W-Well, in that case, I guess I don't 
see any reason for hostility,

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:45.440
and you did pay our bill, so I suppose 
I wouldn't mind showing gratitude!

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:48.550
Do people ever tell you you're easy to handle?

00:11:49.910 --> 00:11:52.060
By the way, who's that young lady?

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:55.810
Tanaka! Who are you? What do you do?

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:59.450
You're asking like someone 
translating a foreign language.

00:11:59.450 --> 00:12:02.060
She claims to have amnesia.

00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:07.350
Hmm, well... For now, you can call me "Gil."

00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:11.370
I'm enjoying life in modern times right now.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:15.880
Still, a girl with amnesia, huh?

00:12:18.150 --> 00:12:23.760
I have knowledge of this era I've been 
summoned to and about the Ainsworth family,

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:26.550
but I don't know anything about you, Tanaka-san.

00:12:26.550 --> 00:12:28.140
You know the Ainsworths?

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:29.640
Know them?

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:33.890
I was summoned by the Cards they created.

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:37.860
They're the ones causing the 
Holy Grail War in this world,

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:39.900
using Miyu as their Holy Grail.

00:12:41.020 --> 00:12:42.060
<i>Miyu!</i>

00:12:42.770 --> 00:12:44.910
Hey, why do you know that name—

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:46.010
I'll destroy them.

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:50.630
I'm here to destroy the Ainsworths.

00:12:51.230 --> 00:12:53.960
I want to rescue Miyu!

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:56.640
Please, if you know where she is, tell me!

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:03.010
You two are really out there.

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:06.220
Destroying the Ainsworths and rescuing Miyu

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:09.180
are practically the same wish.

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:11.640
But how will you achieve that?

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:13.640
Where did your stick go?

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:15.560
Will you go there in your raw flesh?

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:17.780
That would be marching to your death.

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:19.650
But...

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:21.450
Yeah.

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:23.570
It's interesting!

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:25.320
Huh?

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:26.610
Let's go.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:29.910
Well, it's not as if I don't have 
business with them, too.

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:32.120
You'll show us the way?

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:35.570
You should be grateful to this dull, boring city.

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:38.130
Otherwise, I'd never be struck by such a whim.

00:13:38.550 --> 00:13:41.840
We each have our own objectives, 
but we're going to the same place.

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:43.770
I'll lead you there.

00:13:43.770 --> 00:13:48.670
Ainsworth's atelier is in the center of the crater.

00:13:55.280 --> 00:13:58.080
Coats are so warm...

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:02.950
I couldn't leave a cold girl in thin layers.

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:06.280
What financial power and tolerance.

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:10.160
You should have also bought 
proper clothes, Tanaka-san.

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:14.370
Me? I'm nice and toasty, so I'm fine.

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:16.330
Now, then...

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:19.960
Down with the Ainsworths! Let's do this!

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:25.210
<i>She just looks like she's 
heading off to club practice.</i>

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:27.330
We aim for the nationals!

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:29.970
You're not doing this on purpose, 
are you, Tanaka-san?

00:14:33.820 --> 00:14:36.800
Seeing it up close is intense...

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:39.790
Make sure not to accidentally enter the crater.

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:41.900
They'll sense you in a heartbeat.

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:44.020
Th-Then what do we do?

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:47.610
It would be a cinch with Vimana, but...

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:50.390
Hmm, guess the other one has it.

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:52.070
What to do, then?

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:53.700
That won't work, or that.

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:54.570
Not this, either.

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:56.580
<i>Hey, I've seen something like this before...</i>

00:14:54.570 --> 00:14:56.580
Not this. Or this...

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:59.540
Oh, yeah, this should do.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:01.710
Huh? What's that?

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:05.160
I think this is a bit wrong.

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:06.510
What is?

00:15:06.510 --> 00:15:07.970
The way we look.

00:15:08.230 --> 00:15:10.910
But I'm having tons of fun!

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:15.710
You shouldn't be having fun when 
we're storming the enemy base.

00:15:15.710 --> 00:15:17.680
But it's working perfectly.

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:23.940
Anything wrapped in this cloth is perfectly 
concealed, visually and magically.

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:27.440
As long as you remain in it, 
they won't ever sense us.

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:30.000
I understand that,

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.070
but where are we supposed we go?

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:34.910
You said it's in the center of the crater?

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:36.050
But...

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:38.370
There's nothing but wasteland 
as far as you can see.

00:15:39.150 --> 00:15:41.230
We're almost at the center.

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:43.580
Don't make any loud noises past this point.

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:45.840
The cloth won't conceal sound, after all.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:48.760
Huh? S-Sure, but...

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:51.180
Don't worry. Just step forward slowly.

00:15:56.490 --> 00:15:59.700
<i>Wind? Why is there such a warm wind?</i>

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:10.690
Huh?! What's tha—

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:14.200
Yes, loud reactions are also forbidden.

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:16.360
What's going on?

00:16:16.360 --> 00:16:18.950
Nothing was here a second ago!

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:21.330
They make it look like nothing is here.

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:23.830
A blue sky,

00:16:24.470 --> 00:16:26.340
pretty flower gardens,

00:16:26.990 --> 00:16:28.840
a beautiful castle...

00:16:29.270 --> 00:16:32.340
It's like a paradise in another world.

00:16:33.270 --> 00:16:35.310
<i>That's what makes it scary.</i>

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:39.350
<i>The people capable of this are our enemies?</i>

00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:47.900
Why aren't we going inside?

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:51.400
I'm pretty sure it would be bad to 
walk through the front door.

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:55.160
<i>Wait for me, Miyu. I promise I'll find—</i>

00:16:57.320 --> 00:16:59.160
<i>That's the other one who kidnapped Miyu!</i>

00:17:05.010 --> 00:17:07.130
<i>I-If she spots us...</i>

00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:17.560
Nothing here, huh?

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:23.130
Thought I smelled mapo.

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:29.910
Oh, right. It can't conceal scents, either.

00:17:29.910 --> 00:17:33.010
We nearly died again because of mapo!

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:34.770
Either way, we're safe.

00:17:34.770 --> 00:17:36.730
We narrowly avoided a game over.

00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:38.530
Hey, Gil-kun...

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:40.910
Doesn't that door look suspicious?

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:42.430
It does.

00:17:42.430 --> 00:17:45.370
It's hard to believe she'd go 
in and out without reason.

00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:46.980
Let's try going in!

00:18:02.590 --> 00:18:04.270
I guess we were wrong.

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:06.380
I can't imagine Miyu would be here—

00:18:06.380 --> 00:18:07.660
Someone's there.

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:09.440
Huh? Wh-Where?

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:11.240
All the way back there.

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:13.800
There's someone inside.

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:16.610
This door looks like it's for a jail cell.

00:18:16.810 --> 00:18:17.910
Miyu?!

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:20.070
Ah, hold on...

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:22.190
Miyu! Are you in there?

00:18:22.190 --> 00:18:24.200
If you're there, answer me! Miyu!

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:26.480
Who's there?

00:18:27.300 --> 00:18:29.730
A man's voice?

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:33.000
You're not with the Ainsworths, are you?

00:18:33.690 --> 00:18:37.580
Do you all... know Miyu?

00:18:38.370 --> 00:18:40.150
I'm Miyu's friend!

00:18:40.150 --> 00:18:42.050
I came here to rescue Miyu!

00:18:42.230 --> 00:18:44.530
Her friend...

00:18:45.980 --> 00:18:48.480
I see. I get it...

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:51.850
She got her wish.

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:55.040
<i>He's crying?</i>

00:18:56.170 --> 00:18:58.910
I'm Miyu's older brother.

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:01.740
M-Miyu's older brother?

00:19:02.380 --> 00:19:05.370
But then, why are you locked up here?

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:08.680
Because I failed.

00:19:09.380 --> 00:19:13.580
I fought Ainsworth to get Miyu back.

00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:18.730
And I managed to free Miyu from this world.

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:19.900
But...

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:23.250
Miyu's come back here again.

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:28.340
Even after all that, she couldn't 
escape the chains of her fate!

00:19:29.340 --> 00:19:32.770
This is my fate...

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:34.650
Her fate?

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:36.280
I know!

00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:38.400
I'm the worst kind of evil.

00:19:39.020 --> 00:19:41.060
But please... I'm begging you.

00:19:41.060 --> 00:19:42.410
Save Miyu.

00:19:46.230 --> 00:19:50.080
I don't know anything about fate.

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:53.730
Miyu never told me about her past,

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:58.560
and I didn't know Miyu was being held 
captive by something this big.

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:02.010
The Miyu I know

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:06.790
has trouble chatting, and her 
expressions are hard to read.

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:10.300
So, at first, I was a little scared of her.

00:20:12.030 --> 00:20:14.260
But I understand now.

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:16.280
Miyu's just

00:20:16.640 --> 00:20:19.770
really awkward, that's all.

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:24.660
Her feelings are hidden behind 
her clumsy expressions.

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:30.370
When I told her I wanted us to be friends, 
she risked her life living up to those words.

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:34.330
I still don't know much about fate 
or what's what in this world,

00:20:35.190 --> 00:20:38.750
but that's reason enough for me.

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:40.970
I'll save her because she's my friend.

00:20:40.970 --> 00:20:43.510
If anyone wants to make Miyu unhappy,

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:45.280
I definitely won't let them!

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:51.250
Thanks to you,

00:20:51.720 --> 00:20:54.990
half of my wish has already been granted.

00:20:56.940 --> 00:20:58.720
Please go to Miyu.

00:20:59.270 --> 00:21:02.020
You can leave me behind.

00:21:02.020 --> 00:21:04.740
What are you saying? You'll come with us!

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:06.170
I wouldn't.

00:21:06.170 --> 00:21:08.180
That lock is magic.

00:21:08.180 --> 00:21:10.740
Besides, we don't know what traps are—

00:21:16.180 --> 00:21:17.470
Wh-What's that?

00:21:17.470 --> 00:21:19.160
That was close...

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:22.010
Ambushes are for commoners, you know.

00:21:23.310 --> 00:21:26.030
Tell me how you infiltrated us.

00:21:27.380 --> 00:21:29.730
I have rather mixed feelings right now

00:21:29.730 --> 00:21:32.350
about facing off against that visage.

00:21:33.320 --> 00:21:34.870
If you won't answer...

00:21:37.930 --> 00:21:40.260
Then I'll kill you one by one.

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:44.680
Sorry, Illya-san.

00:21:44.680 --> 00:21:46.610
That is my objective.

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:35.970
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:21.580 --> 00:23:23.000
All gates, open!

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:25.300
Don't use my friends without permission,

00:23:25.300 --> 00:23:26.420
you mongrel!

00:23:26.420 --> 00:23:30.050
Just accept that you can't escape.

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:31.590
Rescue Miyu!

00:23:31.590 --> 00:23:33.300
There's someone I want to beat,

00:23:33.200 --> 00:24:00.000
<b>Your True Enemy</b>

00:23:33.300 --> 00:23:35.520
someone I must beat!
